# Flagg fix: make the lying health checks tell the truth

Two health surfaces on flagg report wrong. The 2026-07-31 post-reboot sweep
receipts are in `.brain/tasks/reboot-repair-sweep.svx`.

## Part 1 — session-index-health false red

`/Users/Shared/joelclaw/bin/session-index-health` (LaunchAgent
`com.joelclaw.central.session-index-health`, last exit 1) queries the RETIRED
Typesense collection `runs_dev` and reports `indexed=0` forever, while real
session indexing runs on SQLite (`sessions.db` — find the live path via the
session-index code in this repo; the `session-search` skill and
`packages/`/`scripts/` mention it).

Do: rewrite the script to check the live SQLite index (row count recency /
freshest capture timestamp — pick a check that actually detects a stalled
indexer, not just file existence). Keep the same exit-code contract the
LaunchAgent expects. Kickstart the LaunchAgent and verify it exits 0 with a
truthful report, and that it would exit non-zero if the index were stale
(demonstrate by pointing it at a nonsense path in a one-off dry run, NOT by
breaking the real index).

## Part 2 — health.sh is an auto-recovery script posing as a reporter

`infra/central/scripts/health.sh` writes state and can invoke recovery, and
it still expects retired surfaces (Restate ports 8080/9070, MinIO :9000).

Do: bring it up to date with what actually runs on flagg today (the sweep
table in the receipts file is the ground truth list). Separate concerns:
`health.sh` becomes read-only reporting; recovery actions stay in/move to
`recover.sh` (read both first — preserve existing recovery logic, just stop
health.sh from auto-invoking it silently; a `--repair` opt-in flag is an
acceptable shape). Remove/inert the retired Restate and MinIO checks. Run the
updated health.sh and include its output in your summary.

## Rules

- Repo edits yes, commits no — steering reviews and commits.
- Do not restart healthy services. Do not touch panda.
- No destructive commands; dcg BLOCKED = full stop, report.
- DONE summary: what changed in each file, verification receipts.

## Result (2026-07-31)

Delivered by pi worker (w28:p15), reviewed and committed by steering.
`session-index-health.sh`: retired Typesense `runs_dev` lookup replaced with
the live SQLite index (`~/.joelclaw/search/sessions.db`, COUNT + MAX
captured_at vs raw month-dir mtime; 82k-file scan cut to ~1s; exit contract
kept). Test harness passes; live probe healthy (162,363 rows, lag 0s);
missing-db probe correctly degrades rc=1. `health.sh`: now a read-only
reporter with current flagg checks; auto-recovery machinery removed (the
`com.joelclaw.central.health` job is not loaded on flagg, so the auto-heal
path was dormant); explicit recovery stays in `recover.sh`, untouched.
README updated.

Deploy still needed (root-owned install, no passwordless sudo on flagg):

    sudo install -o root -g wheel -m 0755 \
      infra/central/native/session-index-health.sh \
      /Users/Shared/joelclaw/bin/session-index-health
    sudo launchctl kickstart system/com.joelclaw.central.session-index-health
